One practical way to break out of overthinking or spiraling in the moment is to use a technique called "5-4-3-2-1 grounding." When you notice yourself getting caught up in thoughts, take a deep breath and focus on your five senses. Notice five things you can see around you, four things you can touch or feel, three things you can hear, two things you can smell, and one thing you can taste. This can help bring you back to the present moment and distract you from your thoughts. Another technique is to use a simple mantra or phrase, such as "I've got this" or "I can handle this," to calm yourself down and refocus. Additionally, setting a timer for a short period, like 2-3 minutes, and challenging yourself to focus on a single task or activity during that time can help you build discipline and break the cycle of overthinking. Would you like to try one of these techniques and see how it works for you?

